@*
 * FILE ROLE: Customer area _ViewStart.cshtml — sets the default layout for all views
 *   inside Areas/Customer/Views/**. Because the Customer area has NO area-specific
 *   layout, the "_Layout" reference falls back to Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml,
 *   demonstrating the layout fallback chain.
 *
 * "_Layout" RESOLUTION FOR CUSTOMER AREA VIEWS:
 *   The engine searches for _Layout.cshtml from the view's folder upward:
 *     1. Areas/Customer/Views/Account/_Layout.cshtml    → not found
 *     2. Areas/Customer/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml     → not found (no area layout)
 *     3. Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml                    ← FOUND — root layout used
 *
 *   This fallback to the root layout is deliberate: the Customer portal should look
 *   identical to the main site (same header, navigation, and footer). Only the
 *   Admin area overrides the layout with its own dark-themed chrome.
 *
 * CONTRAST WITH ADMIN AREA:
 *   Admin area:    Areas/Admin/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml EXISTS → uses it
 *   Customer area: Areas/Customer/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml ABSENT → falls back to root
*@

@{
    Layout = "_Layout"; // no area Shared/ layout → falls back to Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml
}
